[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ManualPage" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/components/manual_page.gd" id="1_page"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
title = "OPERATIONS"
body = "1  MOVE                    W A S D
2  PUSH OFF / JUMP          SPACE
3  CROUCH                  CTRL
4  MAGNETIC BOOTS          Q   (disengage in free fall; re-engage on a surface)
5  INTERACT                E
6  FLASHLIGHT              F
7  RELEASE MOUSE           ESC
8  TETHER                  T   (clip to the nearest anchor; press again to release)

MENUS. Wheel or arrow keys move the highlight; middle mouse or Enter selects. PgUp/PgDn scroll the text in manuals and terminals without changing the selected page. Every readout closes with E or Esc from anywhere.

CARRY. E takes an item; right click drops it. Carry one tool at a time. Tools and charged sealant are on the storage rack. Drop tools somewhere reachable when changing them.

WAKE / WATCH. Start at the quarters warning board: WATCH REPORT lists safety readings, reserves, inspection records and known faults. Unlogged inspection means look, not broken. SHIP LOG keeps the history. The binder is in the galley. Use STATUS at a terminal or the galley service-bay panel for detailed readings.

ROUNDS. Bow to stern: cockpit, quarters, life support (scrubber/reclaimer in its side bay), galley, water closet, storage, airlock, engine bay. Scanner + E at each test point logs wear; multimeter + E identifies one hidden fault at a time. Read DIAGNOSTICS before repairs.

WORK. Compare the symptom with STATUS, read the relevant binder page, fetch the tool and check stores. Isolate as required, repair, close the cover and restore service. Verify the fault cleared AND readings recover; repairs and sleep advance the running ship.

TRIAGE. Falling pressure, unsafe oxygen/CO2, dangerous cold and an emptying battery come before routine wear. Leave safe jobs for the next watch; do not sleep through a worsening safety reading. Rations and drinking water are consumed automatically; check reserves on the board and STATUS.

BUNK. E at the quarters bunk sleeps eight hours; this is not a pause. Restore essential breakers and the scrubber, check pressure/air/temperature and battery trend, then rest. On waking, read the board again."
